   -> The real leak: ~/caspar-build 3.3GB (the CasparCG build tree) + 407M apt cache + 79M crash dumps + 183M boost headers. Now excluded -> should land ~4.1GB.
   -> The apt cache leaked because of a real bug: the exclude had TWO patterns on ONE line, and mksquashfs reads one per line, so it matched nothing. Test added so that cannot recur.
   -> STILL ~1.6GB available: var/lib/snapd holds dead snap revisions + bases for the REMOVED firefox snap. Fix is on the build host BEFORE produce (snap remove --purge + refresh.retain=2), not an exclude - excluding leaves broken mount units at boot. Would take the ISO to ~3.0GB.
   -> SEPARATE PROBLEM FOUND: no Chrome binary ships on the ISO (chromium/chrome not installed, .cache excluded), so template thumbnail rendering will fail on a booted ISO. Pre-existing, needs a decision.
