   -> Why: your client/server split is already clean (163 API paths + 21 WS messages is the whole contract), which is the prize people port to get. Also the ISO argument fails - Firefox cannot be removed because your browser SOURCES are Firefox. And performance cannot improve: video never enters the browser.
   -> The one real argument for native: a native window could shape ITSELF and delete ~600-900 lines of the hole-punching hack. Worth ~1 engineer-month, not 40-80.
