when caspar is reloaded it comes back trying to display the compose preview even though im on devices tab. only going to looks and back clears the windows.

the browser window for instance appears over the gui and caspar, but also over the caspars screen consumer that should be always on top as its a pgm screen.

   -> [pasted caspar stacktrace] NOT A CRASH. Caspar logs a full exception + stack for a failed producer, then recovers and answers 404. Line 168508 of log/caspar_2026-07-20.log shows the cause: `PLAY 6-4 DECKLINK 4` -> "DeckLink 8K Pro [4|1080p5000] Could not enable video input" = the powered-off camera. The trailing "File not found." is Caspar mislabelling it. Same single cause as the whole log audit. Caspar did NOT die: its restart at 14:57 was your own Apply (POST /api/caspar-config/apply), and systemd reports NRestarts=0.

   -> [usb audio audible in meters but not on the stream] PARTLY. HONEST ANSWER: your PGM 2 case is NOT explained. The live ADD line for ch3 was captured and is correct - proper AAC codec, no bad -map, stereo layout matching the real channel. Please re-test now your config is back, and if still silent capture it while running.
   -> But the same FAILURE CLASS was found and fixed on PGM 1: the stream layout resolver read only the DECLARED destination layout, while the generator widens the channel to match any CABLED audio output. PGM1 was declared stereo with an 8ch output cabled to it, so the stream blind-remixed a discrete 8-channel bus. Meters still show signal because they read the mixer - silent only when you listen.

   -> [compose preview returns after caspar reload while on devices tab] DONE. The SERVER re-asserted, not the client: it re-applied the persisted layout on every Caspar reconnect unconditionally. Journal proof: holes correctly dark at 14:53 with NO client report for four minutes, then three rects reappearing byte-identical to the pre-clear geometry - that could only come from persistence. The server now skips the re-apply when the client has withdrawn its rects; returning to Looks restores it.
   -> Residual, not fixed: if the KIOSK restarts while the server keeps running, the server still holds the dead page's intent. A Caspar reload does not restart Firefox, so it is outside what you reported.

   -> [browser window covers the pgm screen consumer] DONE, but needs one setting from you. Two faults, both mine from that day: the placement used a resolver whose fallback is literally "the first PGM screen consumer head" (proven live to return DP-0, your program head), and it only ever moved the window, never sized it. Stacking could not save it because the helper promote and the new PGM always-on-top default put both in the same X layer.
   -> Protection is now GEOMETRIC (helper confined to the operator monitor) rather than a stacking race. CAVEAT: this box has no operator monitor configured, so it refuses to place rather than guessing onto PGM - safer, but not yet confined. Set Device View -> GPU port -> Operator monitor for DP-5 to activate it.

   -> ALSO FIXED while here, both found not reported: your YouTube STREAM KEY was being logged in cleartext (journal + 23 times in caspar's log) - masked now, but ROTATE THE KEY. And two consumer-index collisions: the meter consumer shared index 96 with streaming RECORD and is added to every channel on connect, so a record running across a Caspar reconnect would have been silently evicted; DMX shared 97 with RTMP. Moved to 720/721.
